<PARA INFOID = "T060077A228" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "12Sep2003"     INFOTYPE = "PARTS" INDSW = "ON">
<TITLE>Front Speed Sensor &amp; Rotor</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>A semiconductor type speed sensor is mounted to the steering knuckle, and a magnetic rotor is mounted to the inner race of the hub bearing.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "a4740164c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "2.778in" />
</FIGURE>

<MECA ID = "T060077A228A352" UPDATE = "ORIGINAL" LDUP = "28Jan2004"     MECATYPE = "GENERAL" INDSW = "OFF">
<TITLE>Detection Principle</TITLE>
<LIST1 TYPE = "UNORDERED"><ITEM><PTXT>The magnetic rotor consists of rubber filled with magnetic powder, with N and S poles evenly arranged in the circumferential direction (48 poles each for S and N).</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>When the magnetic rotor rotates, changes in the magnetic field are produced; these are detected by the active sensor and output as vehicle speed pulses.</PTXT></ITEM>
<ITEM><PTXT>Compared with the commonly used passive sensor, detection is possible from a vehicle speed of approximately 0km/h.</PTXT></ITEM></LIST1>
<FIGURE>
<GRAPHIC GRAPHICNAME = "k4250108c" WIDTH = "6.917in" HEIGHT = "5.139in" />
</FIGURE>
</MECA>
</PARA>
